// Copy this file to Debug-Local.xcconfig (gitignored) and paste in the
// values `supabase status` prints on your own machine.
//
// This is the config behind the Keepo-Local scheme: the same DEBUG build as
// Debug, pointed at the local `supabase start` stack instead of the hosted
// project. Keeping them apart is the point — there used to be one Debug
// config, so aiming it at hosted (the only way to get a DEBUG build onto a
// real phone) silently took the local stack away from the Simulator too, and
// every casual run wrote to production.
//
// The `$()` in the URL is load-bearing, not a typo. xcconfig treats `//` as
// the start of a comment, so a plain `http://127.0.0.1:54321` is read as
// `http:` and the build gets a nonsense URL with no warning anywhere.
// `$()` expands to nothing and breaks the `//` up so it survives.
//
// 127.0.0.1 means *this device*, so a build using this file only works in
// the Simulator, which shares the Mac's loopback. On a real phone it reaches
// nothing and the app stops at "Couldn't connect" — use the Keepo scheme for
// device builds.
//
// Nothing here is secret: the local stack's anon key is the same fixed demo
// JWT on every machine that runs `supabase start`. It is still not committed,
// because *.xcconfig is gitignored as a category and carving out exceptions
// is how a real key eventually slips through.

SUPABASE_URL = http:/$()/127.0.0.1:54321
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = paste-the-ANON_KEY-from-supabase-status
